# Function Declaration & Calling

Functions are blocks of code that can be called repeatedly. In Go, functions are *first-class citizens* — they can be stored in variables, passed as arguments, and returned from other functions.

## Basic Syntax

```go
func functionName(param1 type1, param2 type2) returnType {
    // function body
    return value
}
```

## Simple Function Examples

```go
// Function with no parameters or return value
func greet() {
    fmt.Println("Hello from a function!")
}

// Function with a parameter
func greetName(name string) {
    fmt.Printf("Hello, %s!\n", name)
}

// Function with a return value
func add(a int, b int) int {
    return a + b
}

// If parameters share the same type, you can shorten it
func multiply(a, b int) int {
    return a * b
}

// Function returning a string
func greetFormal(name string) string {
    return "Welcome, " + name + "!"
}
```

## Calling Functions

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func add(a, b int) int {
    return a + b
}

func greet(name string) string {
    return fmt.Sprintf("Hello, %s!", name)
}

func main() {
    // Call the function and save result
    greetResult := greet("Gopher")
    fmt.Println(greetResult)   // Hello, Gopher!

    // Use return value directly
    fmt.Println(add(3, 4))     // 7
    fmt.Println(add(10, 20))   // 30

    // Store in a variable
    sum := add(100, 200)
    fmt.Println("Sum:", sum)   // Sum: 300
}
```

## Parameters with the Same Type

```go
// Verbose way
func addVerbose(a int, b int, c int) int {
    return a + b + c
}

// Concise way (same type)
func addConcise(a, b, c int) int {
    return a + b + c
}
```

## Function Scope

```go
func calculate(x, y float64) float64 {
    // result only exists inside this function
    result := x*x + y*y
    return result
}

func main() {
    r := calculate(3, 4)
    fmt.Println(r)    // 25
    // fmt.Println(result) // ERROR: undefined result
}
```

## Function Without Return Value

```go
func printBanner(title string) {
    fmt.Println("==================")
    fmt.Println(title)
    fmt.Println("==================")
    // no return statement
}
```

